<Layout title="Acceptable use — Reelkeep" description="Use Reelkeep only for public content you own or have permission to download."><article class="document"><p class="eyebrow">SAVE WITH CARE</p><h1>Acceptable use.</h1><p>Last updated 28 October 2026.</p><p>Only submit content you own or have permission to download. Public visibility does not automatically grant permission to copy, publish or reuse someone’s work. Respect creators’ rights, privacy and the terms that apply to your use.</p><h2>Supported requests</h2><p>One publicly accessible Reel or video post at a time, up to 50 MiB, where an anonymous source request returns a single supported MP4. Public accessibility and download success vary.</p><h2>Limits</h2><p>Do not use this service to access private content, bypass login or CAPTCHA, evade source restrictions, redistribute protected content without permission, automate bulk downloads or circumvent rate limits. The service never asks for Instagram credentials.</p><p>This is a limited experiment on free hosting. Availability, stored-file retention and download capacity are limited. Failed requests may reflect network problems, unsupported formats, source access rules or resource limits; the displayed result explains the available evidence.</p><p>Reelkeep is independent and is not endorsed by Instagram or Meta.</p><p><a href="/">Return to the downloader</a></p></article></Layout>
